; Part of ferrum. MIT licence, see ferrum/LICENSE.
; FIND edge with ALSO MEASURE angle: the left edge of a block (X- face).
; Start above the top, less than step-off #3023 in from the edge, with
; #3024 of straight edge beyond the start towards -Y. Touches the top,
; then the face twice (moving +X), #3024 apart; reports edge_delta #1011
; and edge_angle #1012 (degrees, counter-clockwise positive). With
; #3030 = 0 the active work offset gets X0 at the first touch and Z0 at
; the top; the other axis is not written. The work rotation is written
; only with #3031 = 1. See ferrum_edge_angle.
o<probe_top_left_edge_angle> sub
o10 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    o<probe_top_left_edge_angle> return
o10 endif
o<ferrum_edge_angle> call [0] [-1]
o<probe_top_left_edge_angle> endsub
M2
